      "id": 1,
      "text": "Queen Creek was originally called Rittenhouse after businessman C. Rittenhouse, who built a railroad stop in 1919.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queen_Creek%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name changed to Queen Creek when the nearby Silver Queen Mine rose to prominence, honoring the mine.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://worldofarizona.com/the-story-of-queen-creek-az/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The old Rittenhouse Elementary School, built in 1925, now houses the San Tan Historical Society and sits on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
